 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 520187,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/10933872f5ad8efe.jpg\" alt=\"The graph plots hormone levels on the y-axis versus time of drought on the x-axis. There are four plotted lines for auxin, abscisic acid, cytokinin, and gibberellins. The auxin line starts at a hormone level just above 3 and gradually lowers to a hormone level just below 3 over time. The abscisic acid line starts at a hormone level of 1, jumps to a hormone level of 3, and then gradually rises to above 4 over time. The cytokinin line starts at a hormone level of 2 and gradually rises to a hormone level of about 2.5 over time. The gibberellins line starts at a hormone level of 3, rises slightly above 3, and then lowers to slightly below 3 over time.\"></p>\n<p>When drought conditions are forecast, fields are sprayed with a hormone that will promote a stress response. Considering the results depicted by the graph, make a claim for which of the hormones presented should be sprayed. Support your claim with reasoning.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1016227,
     "content_html": "Gibberellins, to promote plant growth before the plants are damaged."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016228,
     "content_html": "Abscisic acid, to promote plant growth before the plants are damaged."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016229,
     "content_html": "Abscisic acid, to promote protective response to drought before the plants are damaged."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016230,
     "content_html": "Gibberellins, to promote protective response to drought before the plants are damaged."
    }
   ],
